{"abstract":"In this pictorial, we present the process leading to the creation of N/ERWER, an affectively engaging interactive prototype exploring personal domestic grief practices. N/ERV/ER symbolises a physical presence of the Intangible affective experiences associated with grief as an ongoing connection to the deceased in the present. N/ERV/ER was developed in a Research through Design process fueled by both personal accounts and participatory engagements using various design probes exploring experiences of loss following the death of a loved one. In this pictorial, we unfold the theoretical, methodological, and material dimensions of this process to show how designers can accommodate grief in design practice as a way of utilising and materialising the affective forces present in such sensitive contexts.","author_count":3,"contributors":["Ravn, Nicklas Engelbrecht","Sveegaard, Nadja Striib","Fritsch, Jonas"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-759392"],"filters":{"added":"2024-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Affective Interaction Design","Form giving","Grief","Probes","Research through Design"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"materialising affective experiences designing for personal grief practices","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-SA","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1145/3643834.3660753","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-759392","identifier":[{"id":"85200336159","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["itu-31349ac6-5fe1-4699-bc3f-857fdcbe21a7"],"keyword":["Affective Interaction Design","Form-giving","Grief","Probes","Research through Design"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-E26E3C447514774F0AFA0C51CC51C925"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-SA","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1145/3643834.3660753","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Digital Design","IT University of Copenhagen, Digitalization, Democracy, and Governance, Welfare Technology - Policy - People - Practices"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Nicklas Engelbrecht","key":"ravnpau","last":"Ravn","locid":"20685b27-43b0-4170-bcf8-3cc28832d2e7","name":"Ravn, Nicklas Engelbrecht","orcid":"0009-0001-6144-0451","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Nadja Striib","key":"sveegaardpau","last":"Sveegaard","name":"Sveegaard, Nadja Striib","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Jonas","key":"fritschpau","last":"Fritsch","locid":"d37cba38-dff2-4c27-a515-226cfadfd849","name":"Fritsch, Jonas","orcid":"0000-0001-9065-2843","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1145/3643834.3660753","eisbn":["9798400705830"],"pages":"685-698","status":"p","title":"Proceedings of the 2024 ACM Designing Interactive Systems Conference"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85200336159"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-31349ac6-5fe1-4699-bc3f-857fdcbe21a7"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Materialising affective experiences : Designing for personal grief practices","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-759392","year":"2024","yearsub":"2024"}
